{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1621\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications\" or \"<ip>|Potential Okta MFA Bombing via Push Notifications\"\n\nDetects possible MFA fatigue (push bombing) against one user within the search window (15 minutes when scheduled): 5 or more Okta Verify push notifications, or 3 or more pushes together with 2 or more denied, unanswered or abandoned prompts. An inner query counts per user; one alert per user per window, with the counts in the alert text. Risk floor High (75).\n\nFalse positives: users who repeatedly retry sign-in, or a phone without connectivity. Limitation: bursts that straddle two windows are split, which is why the denied/unanswered branch exists.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_okta_mfa_bombing_via_push_notifications.toml",
  "GUID": "8a188024-aec5-5258-b6d2-68ab8941c403",
